IELTS.lesson({"test": 7, "part": 1, "title": "Test 7, Part 1 — the interview", "candidate": "rawan", "script": [{"who": "examiner", "text": "Good morning. Come in, have a seat.", "ar": "صباح الخير. تفضّلي بالدخول واجلسي.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/1b2def3fa2b0b362.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "My name is Mohamad Khorbatli. Can you tell me your full name, please?", "ar": "اسمي محمد خرباطلي. هل يمكنكِ أن تخبريني باسمكِ الكامل من فضلك؟", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/c756d0707f344069.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Rawan Saleh.", "ar": "روان صالح.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/202a3913fa1b9728.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "And what can I call you?", "ar": "وبماذا أناديكِ؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/5085ae49113e09cf.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Rawan is fine.", "ar": "روان تكفي.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/7809f6ee14a67539.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you, Rawan. Can I see your identification, please?", "ar": "شكراً لكِ يا روان. هل يمكنني رؤية هويّتكِ من فضلك؟", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/7986315afde9daa9.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Of course. Here you are.", "ar": "بالتأكيد. تفضّل.", "shot": null, "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/90c4791e3148c41e.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you. That's all fine.", "ar": "شكراً. كل شيء على ما يرام.", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/a65ff8d3eccec277.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Now, in this first part I'd like to ask you some questions about yourself. Let's talk about shopping.", "ar": "الآن، في هذا الجزء الأول أودّ أن أطرح عليكِ بعض الأسئلة عنكِ. لنتحدّث عن التسوّق.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/7def5fcb097c1a53.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you enjoy shopping?", "ar": "هل تستمتعين بالتسوّق؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/4db613247abd5169.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "For some things, honestly. Clothes, no. I find it exhausting and I'll always buy the same thing in a different colour. But a market in Damascus, for food, I could do that for hours and I wouldn't get bored.", "ar": "لبعض الأشياء، بصراحة. الملابس، لا. أجده مرهقاً وأشتري دائماً الشيء نفسه بلون مختلف. لكن سوقاً في دمشق، للطعام، أستطيع أن أفعل ذلك ساعات ولا أملّ.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/0509e0590b6ce3c1.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you prefer shopping online or in shops?", "ar": "هل تفضّلين التسوّق عبر الإنترنت أم في المحلّات؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/50bc76f43deef648.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Online for anything I already know, shops for anything I don't. The thing is, half of what I'd buy online doesn't ship to Syria anyway, so it isn't always a real choice. You end up with whoever a friend knows who's travelling.", "ar": "عبر الإنترنت لكلّ ما أعرفه مسبقاً، وفي المحلّات لكلّ ما لا أعرفه. المسألة أنّ نصف ما قد أشتريه عبر الإنترنت لا يُشحن إلى سوريا أصلاً، فليس خياراً حقيقياً دائماً. ينتهي بكِ الأمر مع أيّ شخص يعرفه صديق ويكون مسافراً.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/44bf15d88cfd8ca3.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Has the way you shop changed in recent years?", "ar": "هل تغيّرت طريقة تسوّقكِ في السنوات الأخيرة؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/dfd14749a68337ef.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "I buy much less, and not for a noble reason. I just got tired of owning things. Actually that's not quite true. I got tired of moving things, which is different, and I've moved flat four times in six years in Damascus.", "ar": "أشتري أقلّ بكثير، ولسبب غير نبيل. تعبت ببساطة من امتلاك الأشياء. في الحقيقة هذا ليس دقيقاً تماماً. تعبت من نقل الأشياء، وهذا مختلف، وقد انتقلت بين الشقق أربع مرّات في ستّ سنوات في دمشق.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/06924b6b8de9ceba.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you think people buy too much?", "ar": "هل تظنّين أنّ الناس يشترون أكثر من اللازم؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/af0456e3d5da9685.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Probably, although I'm not sure I'm allowed an opinion when the reason I buy less is that things in Syria are expensive. I'd like to say it's a principle. People with money buy things. That isn't a moral failing. It's just what money does.", "ar": "على الأرجح، مع أنّني لست واثقة أنّ من حقّي أن يكون لي رأي حين يكون سبب شرائي الأقلّ أنّ الأشياء في سوريا غالية. أودّ أن أقول إنّه مبدأ. من عنده مال يشتري أشياء. هذا ليس خللاً أخلاقياً. هذا ما يفعله المال فحسب.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/48f0582c35e7a170.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Let's move on to talk about saving and spending.", "ar": "لننتقل للحديث عن الادّخار والإنفاق.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/04371fac48a4fb0c.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you find it easy to save money?", "ar": "هل تجدين أنّ ادّخار المال سهل؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/d263bf7b024033aa.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "No, and willpower isn't the problem. When you're paid in one currency and live in Damascus, saving is a decision about which one to be wrong in. I've basically given up on being clever about it.", "ar": "لا، والإرادة ليست هي المشكلة. حين يُدفع لكِ بعملة وتعيشين في دمشق، فإنّ الادّخار قرار بشأن أيّ العملتين تخطئين فيها. تخلّيت أساساً عن محاولة التذاكي في الأمر.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/5059194e07bf88d8.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Did your parents teach you about money?", "ar": "هل علّمكِ والداكِ عن المال؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/bf3a78182bf070ea.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "My father did, in a very specific way. He'd give me the whole month's amount on the first day and then not rescue me. Which was harsh and also the only reason I can run a business in Damascus now, so.", "ar": "أبي فعل، بطريقة محدّدة جداً. كان يعطيني مبلغ الشهر كلّه في اليوم الأوّل ثمّ لا ينقذني. وكان ذلك قاسياً وهو أيضاً السبب الوحيد في أنّني أستطيع أن أدير عملاً في دمشق الآن، فـ.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/e4df229841705d8c.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "What do you usually spend your money on?", "ar": "فيمَ تنفقين مالكِ عادةً؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/a79dc2148baab6d9.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Rent, obviously, and then the two things I won't economise on, which are, I suppose, good coffee and the internet. Everyone I know in Damascus has their two. Nobody's are the same and everybody defends theirs completely seriously.", "ar": "الإيجار طبعاً، ثمّ الشيئان اللذان لا أقتّر فيهما، وهما على ما أظنّ القهوة الجيّدة والإنترنت. كلّ من أعرفه في دمشق له اثنان خاصّان به. ولا يتطابق اثنان لأحدٍ مع أحد، والكلّ يدافع عن اثنيه بجدّية تامّة.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/3993ff812d3a72d6.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Is it important to save for the future?", "ar": "هل من المهمّ الادّخار للمستقبل؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/41309657a6a79033.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "It is, and I'd say it's also a luxury to be able to think that far ahead. Save for the future assumes you know roughly what the future costs. A lot of people in Damascus are budgeting for about three weeks, and that isn't them being careless.", "ar": "نعم، وأقول إنّه أيضاً ترف أن تستطيعي التفكير إلى ذلك الحدّ البعيد. عبارة ادّخر للمستقبل تفترض أنّكِ تعرفين تقريباً كم يكلّف المستقبل. كثير من الناس في دمشق يضعون ميزانيّة لثلاثة أسابيع تقريباً، وهذا ليس استهتاراً منهم.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/66021b6f13af2cf9.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Finally in this part, let's talk about clothes.", "ar": "وأخيراً في هذا الجزء، لنتحدّث عن الملابس.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/f8594681e1a9ec36.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Are clothes important to you?", "ar": "هل الملابس مهمّة بالنسبة لكِ؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/bbaa2de1e32c2097.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Less than they were, honestly. When I started working in Damascus I thought I needed a version of myself that looked professional. Then I realised nobody I work for has ever seen me below the shoulders, so it doesn't matter and I don't bother.", "ar": "أقلّ مما كانت، بصراحة. حين بدأت العمل في دمشق ظننت أنّني أحتاج نسخة منّي تبدو مهنيّة. ثمّ أدركت أنّ لا أحد ممن أعمل لديهم رآني يوماً تحت كتفيّ، فالأمر لا يهمّ ولا أتكلّف له.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/1e690487238d3ed3.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you prefer comfortable clothes or fashionable ones?", "ar": "هل تفضّلين الملابس المريحة أم الأنيقة؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/75ed63d5dc9b84ff.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Comfortable, and I'd have lied about that at twenty-two. The thing is, when you work at home in a Damascus flat the only person judging what you're wearing is you, and it turns out I'm not very strict.", "ar": "المريحة، وكنت سأكذب في هذا في الثانية والعشرين. المسألة أنّكِ حين تعملين في البيت في شقّة في دمشق يكون الشخص الوحيد الذي يحكم على ملابسكِ هو أنتِ، وتبيّن أنّني لست صارمة كثيراً.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/def82783f9b0d9b0.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do you buy clothes often?", "ar": "هل تشترين الملابس كثيراً؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/f040d277e85e69ff.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Rarely, and badly. I buy the same thing in a different colour, which I think I've told you already, so clearly it's bothering me more than I let on. There's one shop near me in Damascus and that's where I go.", "ar": "نادراً، وبشكل سيّئ. أشتري الشيء نفسه بلون مختلف، وأظنّ أنّني قلت لك ذلك سابقاً، فمن الواضح أنّه يزعجني أكثر مما أُظهر. هناك محلّ واحد قربي في دمشق وإليه أذهب.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/784ffd95c0187a7f.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Do people in your country dress differently now from in the past?", "ar": "هل يلبس الناس في بلدكِ بشكل مختلف الآن عمّا كان في الماضي؟", "shot": "examiner", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/04c45c95276fa99b.mp3"}, {"who": "candidate", "text": "Yes and no, right? The street looks different, obviously. But a wedding or an Eid morning looks, I think, almost exactly like my mother's photographs. The occasions kept their clothes even when the ordinary days didn't.", "ar": "نعم ولا، أليس كذلك؟ الشارع يبدو مختلفاً، طبعاً. لكنّ عرساً أو صباح عيد يبدو، في رأيي، شبيهاً تماماً بصور أمي. المناسبات احتفظت بملابسها حتى حين لم تحتفظ بها الأيّام العاديّة.", "shot": "candidate", "sex": "f", "voice": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120", "clip": "../clips/d88ec3996073b8ff.mp3"}, {"who": "examiner", "text": "Thank you. That is the end of Part One.", "ar": "شكراً لكِ. بهذا ينتهي القسم الأول.", "shot": "two", "sex": "m", "voice": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "clip": "../clips/50f379466faf1658.mp3"}], "boxes": [{"q": "Do you enjoy shopping?", "ar": null, "topic": "Shopping", "model": "For some things, honestly. Clothes, no. I find it exhausting and I'll always buy the same thing in a different colour. But a market in Damascus, for food, I could do that for hours and I wouldn't get bored.", "modelBand": 7.0, "why": "Splits the question in two and answers both halves, with a concrete market at the end instead of a general liking."}, {"q": "Do you prefer shopping online or in shops?", "ar": null, "topic": "Shopping", "model": "Online for anything I already know, shops for anything I don't. The thing is, half of what I'd buy online doesn't ship to Syria anyway, so it isn't always a real choice. You end up with whoever a friend knows who's travelling.", "modelBand": 7.0, "why": "Gives the rule, then the reason the rule barely applies here. The friend who is travelling is the whole economy in one clause."}, {"q": "Has the way you shop changed in recent years?", "ar": null, "topic": "Shopping", "model": "I buy much less, and not for a noble reason. I just got tired of owning things. Actually that's not quite true. I got tired of moving things, which is different, and I've moved flat four times in six years in Damascus.", "modelBand": 7.0, "why": "Corrects herself mid-answer and the correction is the better answer. Four moves in six years is the evidence."}, {"q": "Do you think people buy too much?", "ar": null, "topic": "Shopping", "model": "Probably, although I'm not sure I'm allowed an opinion when the reason I buy less is that things in Syria are expensive. I'd like to say it's a principle. People with money buy things. That isn't a moral failing. It's just what money does.", "modelBand": 7.0, "why": "Refuses the credit the question offers her, which is both honest and a stronger answer than taking it."}, {"q": "Do you find it easy to save money?", "ar": null, "topic": "Saving and spending", "model": "No, and willpower isn't the problem. When you're paid in one currency and live in Damascus, saving is a decision about which one to be wrong in. I've basically given up on being clever about it.", "modelBand": 7.0, "why": "Names the real mechanism in one sentence. 'Which one to be wrong in' is the exchange rate described from the inside."}, {"q": "Did your parents teach you about money?", "ar": null, "topic": "Saving and spending", "model": "My father did, in a very specific way. He'd give me the whole month's amount on the first day and then not rescue me. Which was harsh and also the only reason I can run a business in Damascus now, so.", "modelBand": 7.0, "why": "A method, a consequence and a verdict, in that order, ending on a dry 'so'."}, {"q": "What do you usually spend your money on?", "ar": null, "topic": "Saving and spending", "model": "Rent, obviously, and then the two things I won't economise on, which are, I suppose, good coffee and the internet. Everyone I know in Damascus has their two. Nobody's are the same and everybody defends theirs completely seriously.", "modelBand": 7.0, "why": "Two specifics, then a generalisation checked against everyone she knows."}, {"q": "Is it important to save for the future?", "ar": null, "topic": "Saving and spending", "model": "It is, and I'd say it's also a luxury to be able to think that far ahead. Save for the future assumes you know roughly what the future costs. A lot of people in Damascus are budgeting for about three weeks, and that isn't them being careless.", "modelBand": 7.0, "why": "Reframes the question: saving assumes a predictable future. The three weeks is the evidence and it is not an opinion."}, {"q": "Are clothes important to you?", "ar": null, "topic": "Clothes", "model": "Less than they were, honestly. When I started working in Damascus I thought I needed a version of myself that looked professional. Then I realised nobody I work for has ever seen me below the shoulders, so it doesn't matter and I don't bother.", "modelBand": 7.0, "why": "A changed belief with the reason attached, and a last clause that is funny because it is literally true of her work."}, {"q": "Do you prefer comfortable clothes or fashionable ones?", "ar": null, "topic": "Clothes", "model": "Comfortable, and I'd have lied about that at twenty-two. The thing is, when you work at home in a Damascus flat the only person judging what you're wearing is you, and it turns out I'm not very strict.", "modelBand": 7.0, "why": "Admits what she would once have said, then explains what changed. 'Not very strict' is exact."}, {"q": "Do you buy clothes often?", "ar": null, "topic": "Clothes", "model": "Rarely, and badly. I buy the same thing in a different colour, which I think I've told you already, so clearly it's bothering me more than I let on. There's one shop near me in Damascus and that's where I go.", "modelBand": 7.0, "why": "Catches her own repetition, which is a thing speakers do and writers edit out."}, {"q": "Do people in your country dress differently now from in the past?", "ar": null, "topic": "Clothes", "model": "Yes and no, right? The street looks different, obviously. But a wedding or an Eid morning looks, I think, almost exactly like my mother's photographs. The occasions kept their clothes even when the ordinary days didn't.", "modelBand": 7.0, "why": "Separates ordinary days from occasions and supports it with her mother's photographs."}], "voices": {"examiner": "piper-en_GB-alan-medium-s119", "candidate": "piper-en_US-hfc_female-medium-s120"}});
